            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-PHWQdFGsPoGYvaxWWDvlT9XLgch\">Looking at the countries with the most striking figures, the UK imported approximately 80,000 tonnes of tea, which was about twice the amount of coffee it brought in, at roughly 30,000 tonnes. Meanwhile, Germany's coffee imports reached around 50,000 tonnes, notably higher than its tea purchases of 40,000 tonnes.</div>\n</div>",
